      "slug": "jiao-hua-ji",
      "term": "Jiao Hua Ji",
      "definition": "The Chinese name for beggar's chicken, literally meaning beggar's chicken. A Hangzhou dish traditionally cooked by encasing a whole stuffed bird in lotus leaves and clay before burying it in hot coals."
    },
    {
      "slug": "five-spice-blend",
      "term": "Five-Spice",
      "definition": "A Chinese spice blend combining star anise, cloves, cinnamon, Sichuan pepper, and fennel seeds. It gives a warm, complex flavour to braised meats."
    },
    {
      "slug": "marinade-penetration",
      "term": "Marinade Penetration",
      "definition": "The process by which acidic or salty marinade ingredients break down the outer layer of meat and carry flavour inward. Longer marinating times and scoring the meat help penetration."
    }
  ],
