            "text": "Jiao Hua Ji"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " involves a beggar who stole a chicken and, lacking a pot, buried it wrapped in mud and lotus leaves in coals. The result was a bird that steamed in its own juices. This adaptation uses chicken thighs and a dutch oven to recreate that sealed, aromatic environment."
          }
        ]
